      "register": 62,
      "mask": 240,
      "value": 96,
      "net": "RAMP_DONE"
    },
    "ramp_both_channels": {
      "register": 77,
      "and_bit": 2,
      "or_override_bit": 5
    },
    "notes": [
      "Configuration requirements, not an executable register recipe",
      "Preserve reserved bits and configure/verify the complete analog/reference, PCM format, filter, volume and clock-monitor state",
      "Keep direct monitor muted so standalone audio routes through MCU DSP",
      "Never infer bare DAC scale or calibration range from nominal evaluation-board output"
    ]
  },
  "startup_and_fault_requirements": [
    "Hold D0 CODEC_RUN low for at least20ms on startup/reconfiguration; this also holds the three MCP devices in reset",
    "Require hardware CODEC_PGOOD and PRE_ANALOG_OK before raising CODEC_RUN",
    "Initialize MCPs and muted codec, verify0xAF chip ID and all required register readbacks",
    "Start 48kHz/32-bit dual-slave SAI2 with silent output before unmuting the configured DAC",
    "Configure hardware clock-valid and both-channel ramp-done flags; verify real clock/soft-ramp behavior",
    "Read ANALOG_OK high before allowing the existing healthy/rearm logic to generate a fresh D29 permit edge",
    "Drop D29 immediately on any status/read/configuration fault; E02 must continue to clear independently through hardware ANALOG_OK/watchdog",
    "Restart converter qualification after any operation capable of changing analog DC state",
    "Do not wire this profile to the existing D25..D28 control assignment; use its matching carrier and firmware adapter"
  ],
